<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Coles not concerned by retail outlook.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Coles not concerned by retail outlook.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Australian retailer Coles Myer Ltd said on Thursday it was not pessimistic about the retail environment in the second half of the 1996/97 year ending July 27.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't have any unusual pessimism about the second half,&quot; chief executive Dennis Eck told reporters in Melbourne.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't see anything out there that gives us cause for great concern. Our view is that it will be very steady as she goes.....&quot;  </p>
<p>Earlier on Thursday Coles reported a 40.7 percent increase in net profit after abnormals to A$273.6 milion for the 26 weeks to January 26.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
